    "created_at": "2019-07-09T09:31:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-09T09:31:21Z",
    "body": "> I wonder if we should adopt this before the draft standard becomes an actual standard. It might well change and then we'd have even more explaining to do.\r\n\r\nJust as a heads up, the standard has now been [published](https://www.iso.org/standard/70908.html), and the \"X\" character is still used for [`unspecified digits`](https://www.iso.org/obp/ui/#iso:std:iso:8601:-2:ed-1:v1:en)\r\n\r\nAs for the '00', many systems /languages actually have unspecified (or varying) behaviour, when such dates are entered. Maybe '00' was explicitly avoided in order to prevent confusion.\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
