    "created_at": "2019-07-09T12:32:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-07-09T12:32:59Z",
    "body": "Thanks. It's not entirely clear to me what changes are to be made in response to this (assuming implementers are willing to implement this, but I suspect they want to eventually given that it's important for users). Can any number in any date (not time?) become an X? How does this affect operations such as https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#number-of-days-in-month-month-of-year-year?\r\n\r\nSomething like 2019-X7 is presumably invalid as the X must be 0?\r\n\r\nI guess one would have to buy the standard to be really sure? Should this affect JavaScript's `Date` object?",
